Every phone number displayed on the website should be clickable.

On mobile devices, clicking a number should immediately open the phone dialler with the selected number entered.

Use proper tel: links across the website.

5. Add a Downloadable Menu

Add an option for visitors to download the school/menu document once the final file is provided by the client.

The button may be labelled:

Download Menu

The menu should open or download as a PDF file.

Form Validation Improvements
6. Improve Email Validation Across All Forms

Currently, users can enter random or invalid email addresses into the website forms.

Apply email validation to every form on the website.

Required behaviour:

Reject incorrectly formatted email addresses.
Remove unnecessary spaces before or after the email.
Display a clear error message for invalid email formats.
Where genuine email ownership must be confirmed, send an email verification link or one-time code.
Do not treat a submission as verified until the user completes the verification.

Suggested error message:

Please enter a valid email address.

Important: A browser cannot reliably confirm whether every email inbox actually exists. Email-link or OTP verification should be used where ownership confirmation is required.

7. Improve Phone Number Fields Across All Forms

The current phone fields allow users to:

Enter letters.
Enter more digits than permitted.
Submit a number without selecting a country code.
Enter an unverified or invalid number.

Update every phone-number field with the following:

Add a country-code selector.
Allow numbers only.
Prevent letters and unsupported special characters.
Apply the correct minimum and maximum length according to the selected country.
Format the number clearly while the user types.
Display an error for incomplete or invalid numbers.
Where verification is required, send an OTP to verify ownership of the phone number.

Suggested error message:

Please enter a valid phone number.

